# 12. Write a Python program to remove a specific key from a dictionary, retrieve all key-value pairs, and check whether a given key exists. Given Input: car = {"brand": "Toyota", "model": "Camry", "year": 2022, "color": "blue"} 

car = {"brand": "Toyota", "model": "Camry", "year": 2022, "color": "blue"}

del car["color"]

print(car.items())

key = "brand"
print(key in car)